WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.267
I want to go to now

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.036
longtime Putin critic and nemesis

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:03.937
Bill Browder.

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:05.171
He was actually once

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:07.340
the largest foreign investor in Russia.

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:10.010
Now, of course, a wanted man by Putin

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:10.977
And, Bill,

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:12.612
I always appreciate speaking to you.

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:13.980
And I want to start with something

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.248
that I know you understand

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:16.449
better than almost anyone.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:18.418
That St Petersburg official

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:19.619
that I spoke with earlier

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.721
today is now in exile in Georgia,

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.656
but he's speaking out, signed a letter

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.225
asking Putin to free Alexei

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:26.659
Navalny, demanding Russians

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:28.995
have the rights that they deserve.

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:30.330
And he told me some

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.197
who signed that letter

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:32.532
are still in Russia.

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:34.034
How fearful are you for

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:37.037
all of these people's safety?

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:37.904
Very fearful.

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.939
And basically there is no

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.909
willingness on the Putin regime

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:45.145
to tolerate any dissent.

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:47.514
Anybody who says anything like that

00:00:47.514 --> 00:00:48.948
will be put on a list

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:51.251
and those people will become targets.

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:52.452
And so I would imagine

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:53.620
that if anyone who signed

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.488
that letter is still in Russia,

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:56.656
then they'll be a target to either

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:59.392
be arrested or perhaps worse

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:00.794
And you also heard Dimitri say

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:02.362
that he and others

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:03.630
who signed the letter who

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.799
who are not in Russia and of course,

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:07.500
many of them like here in countries

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.769
that are very friendly to Russia

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.271
they're looking forward to returning,

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:12.439
but they need

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:14.040
Putin's regime to fall first.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.241
That's how he put it.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.843
And then he told me something else

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:17.977
about Alexei Navalny.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:19.045
I want to play that for you, Bill.

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:22.916
Navalny is

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:26.086
slowly dying in prison right now,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.056
but I hope that he's strong enough

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:30.990
to survive

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:34.861
until something changes in Russia.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:38.631
And basically, I think he's in prison

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.767
until Putin is in power.

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.671
From what you see, Bill, do you see a day

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:45.505
anytime soon

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:46.739
in the context of this war

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:47.440
and all the failures

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.476
where Putin's regime actually falls?

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.277
Navalny is free.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:52.445
Dmitri and others can return.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.481
Is that day near?

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.717
Well, it's a possibility.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:58.518
But I would

00:01:58.518 --> 00:01:59.219
I hate to say

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:01.321
it's it's a low possibility.

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.924
You know, for example, if if Ukraine

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.293
could push Russia out of Crimea,

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.095
Crimea was such an important thing

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.063
for Putin.

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:11.397
That might be the kind of thing

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:11.831
that would lead

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:13.733
to the Putin regime

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:15.935
fracturing and falling.

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.270
But you also have to understand that

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:18.138
that if

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:19.806
if for some reason that were to happen,

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:21.908
Putin would probably lose his life.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:25.945
And Putin is such a little man right now,

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:27.580
so scared for his own life

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.149
that he's ready to sacrifice

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:30.316
the lives of

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:31.818
hundreds of thousands, perhaps

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:32.952
even millions of men

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.255
to keep this war going, to

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:36.723
keep himself from being defeated.

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:37.624
And so

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:38.291
we have

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:38.992
that's why I say

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:40.527
it's a low probability event

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:42.128
that the regime falls

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:44.164
because Putin will hang on for dear life

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:47.000
and he'll put so much at stake

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.668
in the meantime.

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.136
And of course, assassinations

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:52.205
inside Russia, outside Russia,

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:55.008
using poison is sort of a signature

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:57.810
calling card for Putin's forces.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.646
Navalny, not the only Putin enemy

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:00.713
who has been poisoned.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:02.849
And I actually spoke recently

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:04.184
to the lawyer

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:06.352
and also to the son of the former

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:07.053
president of Georgia,

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:08.154
Mikhail Saakashvili,

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:10.190
who is, of course, a foe of Putin.

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:13.226
And they say he's been poisoned by Putin.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:15.562
They did DNA testing.

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:17.197
They said his arsenic levels were high.

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:18.097
They found a whole lot of other

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:19.465
things as well.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:20.133
I just want to show everyone

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.100
a picture of Saakashvili

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.236
one year ago on the left.

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:24.037
On the right.

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:24.571
There he is.

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:26.172
Recently, he's in prison in Georgia

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:28.007
on abuse of power charges

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:30.343
which he says are false

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:33.213
and politically motivated.

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:34.614
But I want to share with you, Bill,

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:36.249
a letter that I got, a moving

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:37.650
note that I got from Saakashvili

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.751
after I spoke with his lawyer.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:39.886
And I've known Mr.

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:41.654
Saakashvili for a long time.

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.456
You can see from the handwriting here.

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:45.058
And that's

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:46.292
part of what's hard to watch here.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.827
He suffered physical repercussions

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:49.829
and it is hard to look at that.

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:51.197
And people can read it.

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:51.664
He writes,

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:52.432
I really regret

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:53.866
that he didn't see me in Kiev

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:54.834
as I had already gone on

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.836
my ill fated trip.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:57.036
Bill,

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:57.971
do you have any hope

00:03:57.971 --> 00:03:59.172
that Mikheil Saakashvili

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:01.641
will be freed and survive?

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:04.310
Well, I mean, what I what I see is

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:04.978
is something

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:07.380
truly horrific and heartbreaking

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.850
This is a politically motivated arrest

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.885
is being tortured in prison.

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:14.687
The images that you've shown

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:16.889
are deeply disturbing.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.658
I've lived through a similar situation

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:19.692
with my lawyer, Sergei

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:21.995
Magnitsky, who started out healthy

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:23.496
and ended up being tortured

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:23.830
to death

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:26.032
in prison, denied medical care

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:27.900
and dying in prison.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.270
And so for me, this is deja vu.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:32.205
And when I saw those images of

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:33.473
Mikhail Saakashvili,

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:35.742
I spoke out.

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:37.143
And since then,

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:39.012
his team has been in touch with me.

00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:40.613
I'm asking for my help,

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:42.482
asking for begging for my help

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:44.951
to do anything that I can do to help them

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:46.319
get him out of prison.

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:49.188
And it seems to me that he's being held,

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:52.425
I believe, at the behest of Russia.

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:54.460
Vladimir Putin has hated Saakashvili

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.762
since Saakashvili

00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:57.330
stood up to Putin in 2008

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.265
when Russia invaded Georgia.

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:00.533
And Putin.

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:01.834
He never forgets.

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:02.635
He's a vindictive

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:03.936
little man who never forgets.

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:06.706
And what Georgia has to do right now

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:08.474
is release Saakashvili to the west

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:10.209
so he can be treated properly

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:11.611
and he doesn't die.

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:13.713
Because if he were to die in prison,

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:15.014
I believe that this would change

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:16.849
the West's view of Georgia.

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:17.884
For many generations

